Subject: ghostty_surface_synchronized_update says a frame is half drawn

The pty's output reaches the terminal a kilobyte at a time, each piece
under the renderer's lock, so a program's frame of several kilobytes is
on the screen half drawn between pieces. The renderer waits for the end of
a synchronized update (mode 2026) before it draws; an app reading the text
(ghostty_surface_read_text) can't tell. Calm keeps what a full-screen
program shows by reading its screen a few times a second, and a half-drawn
frame read as a new view would be kept twice. A read of the mode under the
renderer's lock, as ghostty_surface_alternate_screen reads the screen.

Calm's own patch (not from thdxg/ghostty); applies on top of 0020.

diff --git a/include/ghostty.h b/include/ghostty.h
--- a/include/ghostty.h
+++ b/include/ghostty.h
@@ -1207,6 +1207,7 @@
 GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_preedit(ghostty_surface_t, const char*, uintptr_t);
 GHOSTTY_API bool ghostty_surface_mouse_captured(ghostty_surface_t);
 GHOSTTY_API bool ghostty_surface_alternate_screen(ghostty_surface_t);
+GHOSTTY_API bool ghostty_surface_synchronized_update(ghostty_surface_t);
 GHOSTTY_API bool ghostty_surface_mark_search_match(ghostty_surface_t,
                                                    ghostty_selection_s);
 GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_clear_search_match(ghostty_surface_t);
diff --git a/src/apprt/embedded.zig b/src/apprt/embedded.zig
--- a/src/apprt/embedded.zig
+++ b/src/apprt/embedded.zig
@@ -2155,6 +2155,13 @@
         return surface.core_surface.alternateScreen();
     }
 
+    /// Whether the program is in the middle of a synchronized update
+    /// (mode 2026). Until it ends, the screen may hold half a frame: the
+    /// renderer waits for it, and so should an app that reads the text.
+    export fn ghostty_surface_synchronized_update(surface: *Surface) bool {
+        return surface.core_surface.synchronizedUpdate();
+    }
+
     /// Paints `sel` as the current search match, the way the search's own
     /// selected match is painted, for an embedder that finds matches
     /// itself (with a regular expression, which the search doesn't take).
diff --git a/src/Surface.zig b/src/Surface.zig
--- a/src/Surface.zig
+++ b/src/Surface.zig
@@ -3910,6 +3910,13 @@
     return self.io.terminal.screens.active_key == .alternate;
 }
 
+/// Returns true while the program draws a synchronized update (mode 2026).
+pub fn synchronizedUpdate(self: *Surface) bool {
+    self.renderer_state.mutex.lockUncancelable(global.io());
+    defer self.renderer_state.mutex.unlock(global.io());
+    return self.io.terminal.modes.get(.synchronized_output);
+}
+
 /// Hands the renderer `match` as the current search match, as the search
 /// thread hands it its own selected match, or clears it with null. The
 /// renderer takes the match's arena.
